 "notes": "The steamer Ramon Membru (1873, 80 x 11 m) lies on her starboard side on sand and dead posidonia at 22 m, rising 3-4 m, about 400 m NE of the Cavalaire harbour entrance. Wreck position, the three white mooring buoys (Ouest, Milieu, Est) and the coast from OpenStreetMap; the hull is drawn along the buoy line (86 deg), which is an assumption, and bow and stern are not told apart because the salvaged wreck is a flattened field of frames and a near-vertical wooden deck (Joncheray and Brunner via nicoblon.free.fr, Port-Cros park sheet). Watch for boat traffic in and out of the harbour.",
